{
  "id": "flashattention3_hardware_breakdown",
  "title": "FlashAttention-3 Hardware Breakdown",
  "category": "architecture_breakdown",
  "domain_taxonomy": "neural_attention",
  "hook_tag": "MEMORY BANDWIDTH HACK",
  "beats": [
    {
      "beat_id": 1,
      "text": "Your H100 GPU spends most of its life idling, starving for data from the memory bus.",
      "visual_focus": "A flickering H100 chip icon with a red 'IDLE' status indicator.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "starving": "#EF4444"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "Memory latency",
        "action_verb": "chokes",
        "direct_object": "compute throughput",
        "anchor_word": "starving",
        "semantic_role": "state_transition"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "grid_memory",
        "title": "THE IDLE PARADOX",
        "sub": "Why your hardware is lying to you",
        "accent_color": "#EF4444",
        "params": {
          "grid_title": "HBM Bandwidth Saturation",
          "active_cell_label": "Compute Stalled",
          "efficiency_label": "20% Utilization"
        }
      },
      "thriller_role": "pattern_interrupt_hook",
      "act": 1
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 2,
      "text": "The villain is the Memory Wall. Your compute cores are stuck in a single-lane highway, waiting for data to crawl from HBM.",
      "visual_focus": "A bottlenecked highway animation showing data packets stuck behind a toll booth.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "Memory Wall": "#F59E0B"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "Memory Wall",
        "action_verb": "strangles",
        "direct_object": "data flow",
        "anchor_word": "bottleneck",
        "semantic_role": "conflict_definition"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "split_flow",
        "title": "THE MEMORY WALL",
        "sub": "Congestion at the HBM interface",
        "accent_color": "#EF4444",
        "params": {}
      },
      "thriller_role": "villain_bottleneck",
      "act": 2
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 3,
      "text": "FlashAttention-3 pivots to asynchronous overlap, treating data movement and matrix math as parallel lanes in a high-speed relay race.",
      "visual_focus": "Split-screen showing data loading and matrix multiplication happening simultaneously.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "asynchronous overlap": "#10B981"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "Asynchrony",
        "action_verb": "decouples",
        "direct_object": "compute from memory",
        "anchor_word": "parallel",
        "semantic_role": "solution_pivot"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "split_flow",
        "title": "ASYNCHRONOUS OVERLAP",
        "sub": "Hiding latency behind computation",
        "accent_color": "#34D399",
        "params": {
          "input_label": "Hardware Thread",
          "router_label": "Async Controller",
          "branch_a_label": "Memory Stream",
          "branch_a_sub": "Prefetching",
          "branch_b_label": "Compute Stream",
          "branch_b_sub": "Warp Execution"
        }
      },
      "thriller_role": "eureka_pivot",
      "act": 3
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 4,
      "text": "By using cp_async to pre-fetch blocks into shared memory, the kernel hides latency behind FP8 matrix operations, keeping SMs constantly busy.",
      "visual_focus": "Code snippet highlighting cp_async and FP8 register usage.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "cp_async": "#3B82F6",
        "FP8": "#3B82F6"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "cp_async",
        "action_verb": "pre-fetches",
        "direct_object": "data blocks",
        "anchor_word": "latency",
        "semantic_role": "mechanism_detail"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
        "layout": "attention_prism_refraction",
        "title": "THE SECRET SAUCE",
        "sub": "cp_async + FP8 precision",
        "accent_color": "#F59E0B",
        "params": {
          "token_label": "FP8 Weight Block",
          "matrix_title": "Tensor Core Throughput"
        }
      },
      "thriller_role": "technical_deep_dive",
      "act": 3
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 5,
      "text": "The result? A massive 1,180 TFLOPS, delivering a 78.8% efficiency gain over standard PyTorch attention implementations.",
      "visual_focus": "A bar chart showing the massive performance jump compared to standard implementations.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "1,180 TFLOPS": "#8B5CF6"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "FlashAttention-3",
        "action_verb": "crushes",
        "direct_object": "previous benchmarks",
        "anchor_word": "efficiency",
        "semantic_role": "victory_payoff"
      },
      "visual_blueprint": {
